You can use the Format String to insert a drop-down list into a cell of a DataTable, a DataList, a
DataStack, or a DataQueue.
Select a cell with the data type String. Right-click it and select Format. Change to the tab Data Type.
Enter several terms of your choice, separated by a semicolon, and not followed by a blank into the text
box Format String to create the drop-down list in the cell of the formatted range into which the user
