Open a List as a Dialog in the Foreground
By default the windows of the objects DataList, DataQueue, DataStack, and DataTable always open in the
background behind any open dialog boxes. This can make working with lists and tables cumbersome at
times as it involves a lot of moving dialog boxes around on screen.
To prevent this, you can also open the DataList, the DataQueue, the DataStack, and the DataTable in the
foreground as a dialog box with the method openDialogBox.
To open our table SteeringTypes as a dialog box in the foreground, we typed in the instructions below into
our method openTableAsDialog.
SteeringTypes.openDialogBox
